              <comment text="//1) Collect deleted edges and their index updates and acquire edge locks"/>
              <comment text="//2) Collect added edges and their index updates and acquire edge locks"/>
              <comment text="//3) Collect all index update for vertices"/>
              <comment text="//4) Acquire index locks (deletions first)"/>
              <comment text="//5) Add relation mutations"/>
              <comment text="//Directionality is not covered"/>
              <comment text="//6) Add index updates"/>
            </codeElement>
          </codeElement>
          <codeElement xsi:type="code:MethodUnit" name="commit" type="/0/@model.0/@codeElement.0/@codeElement.6/@codeElement.53/@codeElement.0">
            <attribute tag="export" value="public"/>
            <source language="java">
              <region file="/0/@model.2/@inventoryElement.6" language="java"/>
            </source>
            <codeElement xsi:type="code:Signature" name="commit">
              <parameterUnit type="/0/@model.0/@codeElement.1/@codeElement.5" kind="return">
                <source language="java">
                  <region language="java"/>
                </source>
              </parameterUnit>
              <parameterUnit name="addedRelations" type="/0/@model.1/@codeElement.187" kind="unknown">
                <source language="java">
                  <region file="/0/@model.2/@inventoryElement.6" language="java"/>
                </source>
              </parameterUnit>
              <parameterUnit name="deletedRelations" type="/0/@model.1/@codeElement.188" kind="unknown">
                <source language="java">
                  <region file="/0/@model.2/@inventoryElement.6" language="java"/>
                </source>
              </parameterUnit>
              <parameterUnit name="tx" type="/0/@model.1/@codeElement.1452" kind="unknown">
                <source language="java">
                  <region file="/0/@model.2/@inventoryElement.6" language="java"/>
                </source>
              </parameterUnit>
            </codeElement>
            <codeElement xsi:type="action:BlockUnit">
              <source language="java">
                <region file="/0/@model.2/@inventoryElement.6" language="java"/>
              </source>
              <comment text="//1. Finalize transaction"/>
              <comment text="//2. Assign TitanVertex IDs"/>
              <comment text="//3. Commit"/>
              <comment text="//3.1 Log transaction (write-ahead log) if enabled"/>
              <comment text="//[FAILURE] Inability to log transaction fails the transaction by escalation since it's likely due to unavailability of primary"/>
              <comment text="//storage backend."/>
              <comment text="//3.2 Commit schema elements and their associated relations in a separate transaction if backend does not support"/>
              <comment text="//    transactional isolation"/>
              <comment text="/*&#xA;                 * On storage without transactional isolation, create separate&#xA;                 * backend transaction for schema aspects to make sure that&#xA;                 * those are persisted prior to and independently of other&#xA;                 * mutations in the tx. If the storage supports transactional&#xA;                 * isolation, then don't create a separate tx.&#xA;                 */"/>
              <comment text="//[FAILURE] If the preparation throws an exception abort directly - nothing persisted since batch-loading cannot be enabled for schema elements"/>
              <comment text="//Roll back schema tx and escalate exception"/>
              <comment text="//[FAILURE] Primary persistence failed => abort and escalate exception, nothing should have been persisted"/>
              <comment text="//[FAILURE] Exceptions during preparation here cause the entire transaction to fail on transactional systems"/>
              <comment text="//or just the non-system part on others. Nothing has been persisted unless batch-loading"/>
              <comment text="//1. Commit storage - failures lead to immediate abort"/>
              <comment text="//1a. Add success message to tx log which will be committed atomically with all transactional changes so that we can recover secondary failures"/>
              <comment text="//    This should not throw an exception since the mutations are just cached. If it does, it will be escalated since its critical"/>
              <comment text="//[FAILURE] If primary storage persistence fails abort directly (only schema could have been persisted)"/>
              <comment text="//2. Commit indexes - [FAILURE] all exceptions are collected and logged but nothing is aborted"/>
              <comment text="//3. Log transaction if configured - [FAILURE] is recorded but does not cause exception"/>
              <comment text="//[FAILURE] An exception here will be logged and not escalated; tx considered success and"/>
              <comment text="// needs to be cleaned up later"/>
              <comment text="//This just closes the transaction since there are no modifications"/>
              <comment text="//Just commit everything at once"/>
              <comment text="//[FAILURE] This case only happens when there are no non-system mutations in which case all changes"/>
              <comment text="//are already flushed. Hence, an exception here is unlikely and should abort"/>
              <comment text="//Clean up any left-over transaction handles"/>
            </codeElement>
          </codeElement>
